{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0","id":233636,"title":"Integrating Oneiromancy into Changeling 2.0","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-18T19:54:42-07:00","id":233636,"title":"Integrating Oneiromancy into Changeling 2.0","content":"So: in 1e, you\u2019ve got this dynamic where a human got abducted by a Keeper and dragged through the Hedge into Arcadia, where he spent some time being toyed with by his Keeper before escaping back to the mortal world\u2026 where he discovers he can enter peoples dreams??? How the heck does <i>that</i> fit in? <br /> <br /> So, a bit of brainstorming: how would you change things in 2.0 so that oneiromancy is less of an \u201cout of left field\u201d thing, and feels more like an integral part of what the game is about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-18-2014, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T19:56:50-07:00","id":233654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0#post233636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So: in 1e, you\u2019ve got this dynamic where a human got abducted by a Keeper and dragged through the Hedge into Arcadia, where he spent some time being toyed with by his Keeper before escaping back to the mortal world\u2026 where he discovers he canenter peoples dreams??? How the heck does <i>that</i> fit in?<br /> <br /> So, a bit of brainstorming: how would you change things in 2.0 so that oneiromancy is less of an \u201cout of left field\u201d thing, and feels more like an integral part of what the game is about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this is just a thought for now but...<br /> <br /> Okay, going off my thought that now, your Seeming represents how you shaped yourself to free yourself(along with Agency), while your Kith, we know, represented how the Keeper changed you, part of this to me is that somehow, you stole the ability on your way out. This would make sense for, in the other thread, how we are interpreting Fairest represent Agency in the new game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:23:04-07:00","id":233683,"title":"","content":"But <i>everybody</i> gets the ability. Why is it so universal? This isn\u2019t <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>, where the fae are <i>natives</i> of the dreamworlds; so why is a connection to human dreams a universal feature of all changelings?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:24:56-07:00","id":233685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233683#post233683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But <i>everybody</i> gets the ability. Why is it so universal? This isn\u2019t <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>, where the fae are <i>natives</i> of the dreamworlds; so why is a connection to human dreams a universal feature of all changelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because connection to dreams is a feature of the Hedge and the Fae and the Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:27:22-07:00","id":233691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233683#post233683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But <i>everybody</i> gets the ability. Why is it so universal? This isn\u2019t <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>, where the fae are <i>natives</i> of the dreamworlds; so why is a connection to human dreams a universal feature of all changelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as we're starting to get manipulating the True Fae's rules against them, perhaps that answers it. <br /> <br /> The manipulation thing itself ties into the Changelings being masters at pledge making. Now, how that ties into dreams, is still a good question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:28:13-07:00","id":233693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233685#post233685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because connection to dreams is a feature of the Hedge and the Fae and the Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh? Not really. I mean, this isn't Boogie(fan line, sorry if its a bad idea to reference that), where the dream world is essentially what made the monsters, or is an inherent part of their being. <br /> <br /> The Hedge, Fae, and Wyrd, its worth pointing out, have rules, through Contracts. Dreams distinctly do not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:29:38-07:00","id":233695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233693#post233693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh? Not really. I mean, this isn't Boogie(fan line, sorry if its a bad idea to reference that), where the dream world is essentially what made the monsters, or is an inherent part of their being.<br /> <br /> The Hedge, Fae, and Wyrd, its worth pointing out, have rules, through Contracts. Dreams distinctly do not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please read the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:34:47-07:00","id":233698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233695#post233695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please read the books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh? The Hedge is the barrier between the realm of Arcadia and our world. How is that dream like? <br /> <br /> All certainly have fairy tale elements, but that's hardly the same as being dream like. <br /> <br /> To explain my rule part(sort of), note in Arcadia, you have to have Contracts with things to get them to work. One has to have a Contract with fire to use it to cook, for example.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the True Fae are... not inherently beings of dreams. Their origin is unknown, and hotly debated. They also do not have to appear in dreams when they appear on Earth, meaning they aren't inherently tied to them through that angle. Arcadia itself isn't inherently dream like just because its chaotic, after all, with some of that chaos just coming from how psychopathic the True Fae. <br /> The Wyrd is more tied to Fate than Dreams, the former being different than the latter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:43:25-07:00","id":233710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233685#post233685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because connection to dreams is a feature of the Hedge and the Fae and the Wyrd.</div> </div> </div> </div>One caveat: why is this so? I\u2019m not saying that it isn\u2019t, or shouldn\u2019t be; I\u2019m just asking what it is about the Wyrd that makes human dreams part of its \u201cturf\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:43:41-07:00","id":233711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233698#post233698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh? The Hedge is the barrier between the realm of Arcadia and our world. How is that dream like?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/changelingcorep124.png\" target=\"_blank\">Please.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/changelingcorep190.png\" target=\"_blank\">Read.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/60527/Dancers-in-the-Dusk\" target=\"_blank\">The books.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T20:45:32-07:00","id":233719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233710#post233710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One caveat: why is this so? I\u2019m not saying that it isn\u2019t, or shouldn\u2019t be; I\u2019m just asking what it is about the Wyrd that makes human dreams part of its \u201cturf\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I mean, maybe that is the case, but having read a fair amount of the books, I haven't spotted that anywhere. I see connections to Contracts, Folklore, and... psychopathic children who never grow up. That's it pretty much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:07:04-07:00","id":233738,"title":"","content":"And \u201cPlease read the books\u201d isn\u2019t an answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:12:27-07:00","id":233742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233711#post233711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/changelingcorep124.png\" target=\"_blank\">Please.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/changelingcorep190.png\" target=\"_blank\">Read.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/60527/Dancers-in-the-Dusk\" target=\"_blank\">The books.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Of those,<br /> <br /> The last is a specific supplement that you shouldn't assume someone has, and judging by the description, is expanded usage of dream rules, not more explanation on why they can manipulate dreams.<br /> First two are much better evidence. Why didn't you quote the sections right off the bat? As yes, I have read the books(although not Dancers at Dusk yet.) Its worth noting however the first is dealing with a Contract, and doesn't really offer an origin, just more examples of the power. <br /> <br /> The second meanwhile offers that there is a connection, but why? I have a suggestion down below, but the OP's original question isn't answered by either of those.<br /> <br /> However, that just begs further questions. They say its dream-like, but the amount of reinforcement for this is... all over the place. Yes, Arcadia is chaotic, but its notable that almost all of that chaos, ironically, comes from the esoteric rules that originate from Contracts and how the True Fae, not dream-logic. I mean, do your dreams involve esoteric contracts and rules all the time? <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd agree the Wyrd does, and am willing to admit the chaotic nature of the Hedge perhaps supports this, but Arcadia itself this is... screwy.<br /> <br /> Also, to quote Dataweaver, your original answer, to be frank, was useless. It offered no evidence for your position, for one. <br /> <br /> To return to the OP, I think the answer I'll give, as this seems to be the book's, is that these aspects are in folklore as well, and embody aspects of the True Fae themselves that bleed out to their followers and setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 08-19-2014, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:25:00-07:00","id":233777,"title":"","content":"I could provide an explanation using <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>\u2019s cosmology (the Gentry are Supernal Gods that the Exarchs just can\u2019t seem to get rid of, and the Supernal Realms are known to be associated with the Astral Realms \u2014 and may even be an extension of them \u2014 so the fact that human dreams, which are also part of the Astral Realms, are connected to Arcadia makes sense); but <b>Changeling</b> ought to be able to explain such a thing without resorting to another game\u2019s cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:29:22-07:00","id":233778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233742#post233742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First are much better evidence. Why didn't you quote the sections right off the bat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because I'm currently in the process of rereading through the entire WoD in discrete gamelines in rough order of bookcount and Changeling is half a line away from my current point and twice the length of spareable Recent Items List space that I have in my PDF reader.<br /> <br /> Because I have sufficient experience with Citation Wars that I have minimal patience for arguments that require me to pick through over seven books for <i>specific</i> references to a concept that I remember specific instances of <i>existing</i> in sufficient quantity that I know the concept is holistically clearly present.<br /> <br /> Because Dropbox has a fixed spacecount that I don't feel like exhausting in the name of screencapping things for the sake of potentially unappreciative strangers.<br /> <br /> Because it's late and I have work tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Because the corebook has an index and you presumably possess the corebook and the ability to look up the dreamscaping section.<br /> <br /> Because protracted arguments are a thing I am vehemently against and it is easier for you to either follow or ignore my brief exhortation and save everybody a lot of time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, to quote Dataweaver, your original answer, to be frank, was useless. </div> </div> </div>Data has previously decried citation of specific instances as nitpicking and reaching for obscure supplements. To be frank, I don't come to question-threads to debate things with people who don't take the time to actually <i>read the books under discussion and endeavor to process the content thereof</i> and proceed from that lack-of-reading to picking at <i>other people's</i> answers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It offered no evidence for your position, for one. </div> </div> </div>It can be assumed that you have eyes and a brain. I possess far less time than I would like to break my schedule for the sake of getting embroiled in this nonsense where you believe I have a <i>position</i> other than &quot;it's in the books and you can read it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Any further consideration I had for going through the books to find notation that clarified the connection between dreams and Faerie prior to starting and completing my reread of Changeling on schedule maybe a month from now has been exhausted. Done with this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-19-2014, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:33:58-07:00","id":233781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233777#post233777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could provide an explanation using <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>\u2019s cosmology (the Gentry are Supernal Gods that the Exarchs just can\u2019t seem to get rid of, and the Supernal Realms are known to be associated with the Astral Realms \u2014 and may even be an extension of them \u2014 so the fact that human dreams, which are also part of the Astral Realms, are connected to Arcadia makes sense); but <b>Changeling</b> ought to be able to explain such a thing without resorting to another game\u2019s cosmology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points, especially as it really wouldn't make sense to have something so important for the setting be... tied to another cosmology. <br /> <br /> I mean, yes, to be fair to the original authors, perhaps its supposed to be mysterious, but we have good reasons for the Contracts, it has more examples than the dream-logic by contrast does. <br /> <br /> But okay, for another reason... hmm. Perhaps it ties into the origin of the True Fae? Granted, that doesn't make sense as that's supposed to be rather... open to debate for various reasons so... hmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 08-19-2014, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:09:09-07:00","id":233838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233781#post233781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But okay, for another reason... hmm. Perhaps it ties into the origin of the True Fae? Granted, that doesn't make sense as that's supposed to be rather... open to debate for various reasons so... hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pull from Neil Gaiman's Sandman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandman, Brief Lives 5</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>I know how gods begin, Roger. We start as dreams.</b><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> Then we walk out of dreams into the land. We are worshipped and loved, and take power to ourselves. And then one day there's no one left to worship us. And in the end, each little god and goddess takes its last journey back into dreams \u2026 </span></span></span><b>and what comes after, not even we know.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Or, to be clearer: perhaps the Gentry, indeed perhaps Arcadia itself, would not exist if not for the dreams of mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:15:43-07:00","id":233843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233838#post233838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pull from Neil Gaiman's Sandman.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>See, while this works, my problem with it is just that it takes away mystery from the True Fae, To be fair, one could argue, <br /> <br /> A. They don't have to originate from dreams here, as it could tie instead into some sort of more belief centric system relating to this. <br /> <br /> B. They do, but that's still a wide variety of possibilities, seeing as those dreams could be mixing with cultural beliefs to birth them, among other things. <br /> <br /> So... this may be the best reason, but its an imperfect one I guess is my point. Still, you have a good point.<br /> <br /> <br /> On another note, the OP's issue, of it coming out of left field, I've come to realize more re-checking parts of the core book. I mean, its worth noting that, while the Wyrd can also manipulate Fate, but that requires a Contract in the core book, (there may be a supplement that screws with this, sorry on that one if I miss something). Why can Changelings manipulate Dreams without a Contract? Why is Faire magic willing to allow this, but little else without a Contract? <br /> <br /> If it did require a Contract, it'd be a power explained by the explanation for Contracts but... that isn't the case. Ouch. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:22:21-07:00","id":233846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233838#post233838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, to be clearer: perhaps the Gentry, indeed perhaps Arcadia itself, would not exist if not for the dreams of mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more flexible, to be fair, (although then why is Arcadia Contract dependent? That's not a really dream thing, but honestly, that's a debate I'm willing to drop in advance). And... yeah, its a good one, I'll wait to hear though what Dataweaver thinks of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:28:24-07:00","id":233872,"title":"","content":"Don\u2019t. I\u2019m trying to spur discussion here, not railroad my own opinions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:39:29-07:00","id":233878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233872#post233872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t. I\u2019m trying to spur discussion here, not railroad my own opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, k. Sorry guys.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Well, okay, so, we have the True Fae reasoning, which works, but is imperfect, (not terrible mind you.)<br /> <br /> Another idea perhaps is this.<br /> <br /> 2.0 may introduce the idea of Seemings being how one literally changed themselves to get out of Arcadia. This to me would be a physical, mental, and, of course, magical undertaking. The second, the mental transformation, could partially be learning to control one's own dreams, so Changelings could free themselves of the True Fae's psychological manipulations, and with access to magic, that could extend to others. To further support this, assuming Changelings still get glamour from Emotion, they could use similar links to get inside the dreams of humans. <br /> <br /> Now, how does this link to the True Fae? Well, we already know the True Fae can change their form quite freely within Arcadia, giving some of the ability Changelings have(although I'd argue not as much, because they're still limited by lacking creativity), to change themselves. This could allow them to control dreams, along with them probably having similar possible magical links to humans. Perhaps they require Loyalists or Privateers to get the necessary links?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T23:18:14-07:00","id":233901,"title":"","content":"You know, one thing that I really loved from Dancers in the Dusk were the Goblin Miners-because they emphasized and at the same time completely crashed the cosmology of Changeling. For those that don't have that, the Goblin Miners were Hobgoblins that began digging in the Hedge and dug their way into dreams within the Skein, where they would harvest dreamstones, take them back, and sell them.<br /> <br /> Keep this in mind.<br /> <br /> The biggest reason presented in the first corebook for traipsing the dreamscape was because that was where the True Fae worked first, conventionally. I don't think it was ever squared away if they were Skein-walking or doing the same sort of stuff the Lost were doing, but either way, it was the frontlines, the borders where the True Fae were first held off. They would go and seed the dreams, poisoning them, haunting them, and manipulating them-to the point of controlling them in their sleep.<br /> <br /> See a connection?<br /> <br /> You want me to functionally connect them all together(Hedge, Arcadia, Dreams?), can't help you, but I like the idea that the presence of the fae warps dreams. If you don't watch that stuff, the fae starts leaking out of dreams into reality.<br /> <br /> If you run along with the idea I presented in the Inspiration from Demon thread(Which David might not be), this also creates a terrifying point-if a changeling doesn't master their own dreams, handle the fear in their head, then it will manifest and become real. Changelings in the old edition were masters of their own dreams-I like them being adroit with it, but perfect control? Nah-some of the first dream adventures should be in motley mate's heads.<br /> <br /> Compounding the problem in the last one, If changelings warp the dreams of people around them, it seems fair that it can go both ways. A changeling is connected to the dreamscape in ways others aren't, so a changeling is prone to having other dreams mix with theirs. The thing that makes them adroit with it also leaves them vulnerable. It's a thing you have to watch-constantly.<br /> <br /> Feeling the paranoia build? See the shadows grows? Worry about the glint of white you see in them? How big was it? How many were there? Were you only looking at that shadow? You're so sure something just moved behind you, but you see the smiles there.<br /> <br /> When does paranoia become a real threat? When do real threats become just paranoia?<br /> <br /> Hope you have the Clarity to see the answers. It's a long way home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T01:10:45-07:00","id":233960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0#post233636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So: in 1e, you\u2019ve got this dynamic where a human got abducted by a Keeper and dragged through the Hedge into Arcadia, where he spent some time being toyed with by his Keeper before escaping back to the mortal world\u2026 where he discovers he can enter peoples dreams??? How the heck does <i>that</i> fit in?<br /> <br /> So, a bit of brainstorming: how would you change things in 2.0 so that oneiromancy is less of an \u201cout of left field\u201d thing, and feels more like an integral part of what the game is about?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For what it's worth, one of my writers is talking about wanting to marry oneiromancy into the core template a little deeper, and give it more robust rules. I told her I'd find her the space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T02:17:27-07:00","id":233976,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s worth a lot; thanks for being understanding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T08:53:16-07:00","id":234251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0#post233636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So: in 1e, you\u2019ve got this dynamic where a human got abducted by a Keeper and dragged through the Hedge into Arcadia, where he spent some time being toyed with by his Keeper before escaping back to the mortal world\u2026 where he discovers he can enter peoples dreams??? How the heck does <i>that</i> fit in?<br /> <br /> So, a bit of brainstorming: how would you change things in 2.0 so that oneiromancy is less of an \u201cout of left field\u201d thing, and feels more like an integral part of what the game is about?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is an unavoidable and also tantalizing theme in the WOD that the universe gets processed into a different story by thinking slivers of the known world. So you have Mages, Changelings, Vampires, that all can tell you exactly how the world works (and how everyone else has really messed up the story.) Even then, you can split the story again between all Vampires into the ways &quot;things work best&quot;.<br /> <br /> Gamers then have a heck of a time trying to resolve all the inherent conflicts. It really cannot be resolved. I think that's the point.<br /> <br /> All that said, the Dreamscapes offer plenty of mystery and not much to hang a method upon. Likewise the Keepers are mysterious and most of those who play Changeling seem to like it that way.<br /> <br /> I think, if you want to retain the 'Lost' theme as the central focus of Changeling, you are doing well to retain the Mystery of the abduction/durance/nightmare of what has happened to your character. Which is not to say that &quot;out of left field&quot; is there for its own sake. However, part of horror and trials and really being Lost is that what has happened to you does not make sense. It is not fair. It is madness.<br /> <br /> Wasn't the world supposed to be fair? Was science and civilization telling us life was fair?<br /> <br /> Dreams/Nightmares are some central Mystery to the Keepers themselves.<br /> <br /> I suggest that you take Dreams/Nightmares and imagine the earliest being we would call &quot;person&quot;. Before civilization may we assume there were Dreams.<br /> <br /> When mortals were hunted by beasts and lightning and hunger, there were Dreams. <br /> And when miracles saved 'persons' from the Threats, there were miracles and guardians.<br /> And when 'persons' slept in huddles or caves, they dreamed again of Threats and Guardians.<br /> <br /> So I think Dreams are primary to the human condition, yet something about Dreams has changed enough that Keepers are Fiddling with the mix. Looking to 'engineer a better Dreamscape' perhaps (like science is trying to engineer better food, better medicine? only use the analogy if you like it otherwise, meh.)<br /> <br /> The Lost become attuned to Dreams as they are tampered with. And now can see Dreams like an additional sense. Actually being canny at Dreamwork is another matter.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Arref</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><i>......making magic since 1154 B.C.</i></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2062-arref","name":"Arref","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:36:41-07:00","id":234288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arref</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=234251#post234251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suggest that you take Dreams/Nightmares and imagine the earliest being we would call &quot;person&quot;. Before civilization may we assume there were Dreams.<br /> <br /> When mortals were hunted by beasts and lightning and hunger, there were Dreams.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;attempted humor&gt;Clearly, the reason Fae and Changelings exist is therefore Werewolves.&lt;/attempted humor&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:55:00-07:00","id":234328,"title":"","content":"I feel late to the party, and I'm not going to let that stop me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lets say you're an abuse survivor. Your tormenter is behind bars and you've moved to another country. You've escaped, you're safe but you can't shake this little nagging feeling.<br /> <br /> The danger isn't real, but you feel afraid anyway.<br /> <br /> In short, you're having trouble telling the what's real.<br /> <br /> In Changeling: the Lost, the inability to tell what's real is called Clarity. I don't think I need a citation to claim that it's an important part of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> So: A Changeling can't tell what's real and what's not real. Dreams aren't real, but Changeling's can't tell that. To the lost Dreams are real, and that is why it's a universal power for all Changelings.<br /> <br /> But where as the mortal abuse survivor is just factually wrong to feel threatened, it's not so simple for faeries with actual supernatural powers. Dreams are real to them; if you prick them with a dream thorn do they not bleed? If you feed them with dream food they are nourished.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233960#post233960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, one of my writers is talking about wanting to marry oneiromancy into the core template a little deeper, and give it more robust rules. I told her I'd find her the space.</div> </div> </div> </div>I approve highly, and while we're on the subject. Can I please beseach you to remove meditation from oneiromancy. It just feels so un-faerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:03:24-07:00","id":234340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=234328#post234328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I approve highly, and while we're on the subject. Can I please beseach you to remove meditation from oneiromancy. It just feels so un-faerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly agree on the surface. Still, I thought that was in a broader context of &quot;things that move a Changeling's consciousness beyond clear and cogent -- waking -- thought.&quot;<br /> <br /> ... Actually, come to think of it, I'm not sure I remember reading anything in that vein ever. &gt;.&gt; Though if it wasn't, I do feel it makes sense as a consideration, the idea of some possible capacity for oneiromancy if in an altered state of consciousness. I don't know if meditation bothers me through that lens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T10:19:41-07:00","id":234363,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the rule was &quot;only meditation while in the hedge&quot;. Though if meditation was one of a list of options, I'd be fine with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:42:32-07:00","id":234449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=234328#post234328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel late to the party, and I'm not going to let that stop me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lets say you're an abuse survivor. Your tormenter is behind bars and you've moved to another country. You've escaped, you're safe but you can't shake this little nagging feeling.<br /> <br /> The danger isn't real, but you feel afraid anyway.<br /> <br /> In short, you're having trouble telling the what's real.<br /> <br /> In Changeling: the Lost, the inability to tell what's real is called Clarity. I don't think I need a citation to claim that it's an important part of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> So: A Changeling can't tell what's real and what's not real. Dreams aren't real, but Changeling's can't tell that. To the lost Dreams are real, and that is why it's a universal power for all Changelings.<br /> <br /> But where as the mortal abuse survivor is just factually wrong to feel threatened, it's not so simple for faeries with actual supernatural powers. Dreams are real to them; if you prick them with a dream thorn do they not bleed? If you feed them with dream food they are nourished.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I approve highly, and while we're on the subject. Can I please beseach you to remove meditation from oneiromancy. It just feels so un-faerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like this argument and... wish I had thought of it, along with, of course, that Changelings already can do things like harvest emotions, suggesting they can forge personal links, sort of, which would allow dreams. <br /> <br /> And for the latter, I'm all for making it more an option than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T16:32:44-07:00","id":234789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=234328#post234328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I approve highly, and while we're on the subject. Can I please beseach you to remove meditation from oneiromancy. It just feels so un-faerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>When I think meditation for Changeling, I think dervishes, less yogis. I'll bring it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T01:26:01-07:00","id":235184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233683#post233683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But <i>everybody</i> gets the ability. Why is it so universal? This isn\u2019t <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>, where the fae are <i>natives</i> of the dreamworlds; so why is a connection to human dreams a universal feature of all changelings?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not. It is potentially something any changeling can practice and become proficient at, but by default you can guard the sleep of those you swear to protect - strictly because you know their dreams are in danger from the Fey - and that's pretty much it.It takes learning a contract or engaging in shaky, dangerous vision quests and sorcery to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=234328#post234328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I approve highly, and while we're on the subject. Can I please beseach you to remove meditation from oneiromancy. It just feels so un-faerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aye. The meditation rules were, seemingly, to create a universal set used across all splats. Meditation and waking dreams are the same for changelings, mages, werewolves, and humans. It even sort of touches on this in the mage core, where they establish that mages go through the exact same steps as the lost, they can just go further.<br /> <br /> It's never elaborated on though; You've got two templates that use it directly and each have their own specialty, you have a merit that lets anyone else also do it but not be proficient, and thats it. A more unified system would be welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3652,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3652-siuis","user":"SiuiS","date":". 08-20-2014, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3652-siuis","name":"SiuiS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T10:13:10-07:00","id":235526,"title":"","content":"I actually went into this thread ready to argue that Dreams were no more thematic for Changeling than any other Contract, and as such Oneiromancy should be folded into Contracts of Dreams ...<br /> <br /> ... but actually, darn, that <i>really</i> ties in brilliantly with the abuse-victim metaphor. Thanks, King!<br /> <br /> So now, I find myself thinking that the opposite is true, and it should definitely be a core part of the template. Specifically, it should be something you .<br /> <br /> Every night - or perhaps just whenever they have especially vivid/Arcadian dreams, or dream of their Durance and their Keeper - Changelings dreamwalk. It might just be a question of quickly noting what you dreamed about, or it might be an entire Chronicle set in dreams and bookended by the waking world, depending on how much Oneiromancy the players and Storyteller want in their game. But your dreams should haunt you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":".  stupid phone can't format text 08-23-2014, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T11:14:20-07:00","id":235591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=234789#post234789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I think meditation for Changeling, I think dervishes, less yogis. I'll bring it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>fairies have a noted historical fondness for all night ragers filled with circular dancing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T13:02:49-07:00","id":235694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=235526#post235526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually went into this thread ready to argue that Dreams were no more thematic for Changeling than any other Contract, and as such Oneiromancy should be folded into Contracts of Dreams \u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026 but actually, darn, that <i>really</i> ties in brilliantly with the abuse-victim metaphor. Thanks, King!<br /> <br /> So now, I find myself thinking that the opposite is true, and it should definitely be a core part of the template. Specifically, it should be something you <i>can\u2019t opt out of</i>.<br /> <br /> Every night - or perhaps just whenever they have especially vivid/Arcadian dreams, or dream of their Durance and their Keeper - Changelings dreamwalk. It might just be a question of quickly noting what you dreamed about, or it might be an entire Chronicle set in dreams and bookended by the waking world, depending on how much Oneiromancy the players and Storyteller want in their game. But your dreams should haunt you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires have to feed. Werewolves have to hunt. Mages (presumably) have to research.<br /> <br /> Changelings have to dream?<br /> <br /> I'm intrigued. Not convinced, mind you, but definitely intrigued.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T21:47:54-07:00","id":236178,"title":"","content":"To again steal from the Sandman, Dreams are tied to stories. Stories come from the imagination, and Dreams are the raw stuff of imagination. The Gentry literally depend on stories to maintain their very existence. They turn to dreams to find the inspiration they themselves do not possess inherently. Dreams are also a vital source of Glamour, which is essentially distilled base human emotion (Dreams being expressions of the unconscious are gonna be loaded with the stuff!). If you want to fit this into the overarcing mythology, consider that Gentry need names to remain in existence. Without a True Name a Gentry simply ceases to be, or at best changes into an entirely different state of being. To maintain cohesion, to BE what they want instead of given over to the mad whims of the Wyrd, a Gentry must acquire a Name. And then it must find a Title to give itself further cohesion and existence. Contracts are an expression of this process...they give the Gentry definition and existence. Glamour (and by extension Dreams) are the other side of the coin. They are the raw energy of possibility, ready to be shaped by the Fae and the Wyrd into a defined state of being through a Contract. To put it still another way, perhaps Gentry literally ARE dreams and glamour, ones that managed to staple down their own existence with a Name and Contracts instead of being a fleeting thought in the dance of the Wyrd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T22:46:20-07:00","id":236207,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not fond of the notion that the Gentry are <i>dreams</i>; that\u2019s perhaps a bit too <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>. But I could see going with the notion that they\u2019re <i>living stories</i>, and that a changeling\u2019s ability to enter dreams is connected to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T08:08:56-07:00","id":236506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=236207#post236207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not fond of the notion that the Gentry are <i>dreams</i>; that\u2019s perhaps a bit too <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>. But I could see going with the notion that they\u2019re <i>living stories</i>, and that a changeling\u2019s ability to enter dreams is connected to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The living stories concept works a bit better, as it also connects to how Wyrd's connected to Fate, and the various folklore aspects Changeling the Lost has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T09:54:15-07:00","id":236621,"title":"","content":"Random idea. Nix the whole turn-any-door-into-a-gate thing. Physical gates exist. Known ones are almost always squatted by the Court(s) and protected jealously, especially if its near useful Hollows or Trods. A Changeling without a gate (or the Court's permission to use it) can enter the Skein. From there, they can enter the Hedge. Maybe require a link to someone specific (probably requiring touch, a token, or some other magic) in order to cross from their dream into the Hedge. Make it so Changelings don't have personal dreams of their own. When they sleep, they go to &quot;The Skein&quot; naturally. There probably needs to be a mechanic for forcing yourself asleep. Possibly being mandatory, and at some cost.<br /> <br /> To clarify. I'm suggesting that Arcadia and the Mortal World be two points on the map. The Hedge is the rock and pirahna infested river that connects them. Dreams are the boat people ride in (when not just walking through an open gate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-21-2014, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T09:59:14-07:00","id":236626,"title":"","content":"In terms of rules. <br /> <br /> Please focus on scope and elegance over depth for the core rules. Oneiromancy only matters in the context that it affects the physical world. Using Oneiromancy to get information or inflict conditions is great. Rules for &quot;Dream Combat&quot; more complicated than an extended and contested action (think Lashing Out), probably is not. As an ST I need to be able to control how much spotlight the Oneiromancer gets. &quot;Use this power, now the ST needs to run a personal scene for just you&quot;&quot; hurts that. I can be particularly lavishing with my extended action roll descriptions if the situation calls for it. I think there may be a danger of inheriting issues Shadowrun has with the Matrix and/or Astral if you treat Oneiromancy as a whole seperate world or state of being. Not to say Shadowrun isn't a good game, but it has to jump through a lot of hoops to acomodate its three world design decisions.<br /> <br /> That said, if you were to release &quot;Skeinwalkers: Adventures in Dreamland&quot; that expanded on the rules and let ST run entire Stories through Oneiromancy, I'd probably buy that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T15:38:04-07:00","id":237005,"title":"","content":"Dave has said something about M2e having \u201cDown and Dirty spellcasting\u201d, or something to that effect; C2e could do well with \u201cDown and Dirty Oneiromancy\u201d for similar cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T17:06:41-07:00","id":237520,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> I agree with that, I'd prefer Oneiromancy have the same complex rules that allow for entire chronicles to revolve around it by default, but have a 'down and dirty' version for simple 'dream readings' or minor manipulations.<br /> <br /> That said, I know 2e isn't on average seeming to focus too much on crossover rules, but PLEASE make sure Astral rules and Oneiromancy rules (and any other dream sytems) are more easily compatible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T07:12:25-07:00","id":238170,"title":"","content":"If a set of mechanics is mutually exclusive with the &quot;normal&quot; focus of a chronicle and robust enough to have seperate chronicles written about it, then that set of mechanics deserves its own supplement. &quot;Oneiromancy as it relates to the real world, nothing else&quot; should be the default and what is in the core. &quot;Oneiromancy as this whole other thing that you could optionally focus entire campaigns around&quot; should come later. Don't get me wrong, I'm totally for inception changeling. I think you could do some great stuff by expanding Oneiromancy. But if you don't start with &quot;How Oneiromancy feeds into the normal themes and settings the players are meant to play in' then Oneiromancy will wind up one of those things people think is cool but never really sees much play outside of campaigns specifically designed to focus on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T07:45:56-07:00","id":238185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=236621#post236621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random idea. Nix the whole turn-any-door-into-a-gate thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I love that! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T14:31:59-07:00","id":238532,"title":"","content":"OK, this is at least my fifth time attempting to write this comment. Gah. This text editor has passed beyond merely broken, and is now actively fighting me.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/5CN5shzQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/5CN5shzQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://pastebin.com/5CN5shzQ\" target=\"_blank\"> http://pastebin.com/5CN5shzQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 08-23-2014, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T10:44:36-07:00","id":239325,"title":"","content":"I meant it more in terms of 2e Vampires regularly play a feeding scene; 2e Werewolves will probably regularly play a hunting scene; etc. Which goes to 2e Changelings regularly playing a dreaming scene. V:tR2e recommends that you start out a session with a quick feeding scene; I wouldn't be opposed to seeing the same recommendation for Changelings, where they quickly run through a dreaming scene, and perhaps harvest some Glamour naturally that way.<br /> <br /> And it would even make sense; Glamour, in addition to being necessary for survival, is a reminder that they're part Fae. It makes sense that they'd harvest it as part of a recollection of their Durance. (Just like watching someone eat a normal meal is a suggested breaking point for Vampires.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T08:40:51-07:00","id":240343,"title":"","content":"Oh, indeed! Good point, I think that would work really well with the game's themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T06:17:45-07:00","id":244762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=236207#post236207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not fond of the notion that the Gentry are <i>dreams</i>; that\u2019s perhaps a bit too <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>. But I could see going with the notion that they\u2019re <i>living stories</i>, and that a changeling\u2019s ability to enter dreams is connected to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally like this explanation, possibly in part because I've been binge reading sandman for a while but it also feels like it fits changeling and reinforces the way the True Fae are tied to the wyrd and its love of stories. The wyrd also sort of makes sense to be strongly bound up in humanity's collective unconcious since, as changelings interact with it, human dreams basically function as a network if interconnected stories mostly based on strong emotions, memories of the past and omens of the future.<br /> <br /> Minor tangent on that subject: I spoke to Dave Brookshaw at Gen Con about Beast: the Primordial asking specifically about what level of the astral in Mage terms beasts interact with, and the short version as far as I can tell is basically &quot;all of them at once and sometimes multiple levels simultaneously.&quot; The official word is that the astral works the way it does for mages because the people looking at it are mages so they'll interact with it in a way that makes sense to mages, and beasts will look at it from a completely different angle. Perhaps there is some fun to be had with how changelings view the whole of the astral/skein (probably by expanding on the ideas in swords at dawn and dancers in the dusk) in the new edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T22:39:12-07:00","id":294535,"title":"","content":"Popping back in because it's been well over a month and a lot has happened, most prominent being that I finished my reread of the corebook today, so\u2026 have a big box and a small summation:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">What is an explicit outcome of bottoming out on Clarity as described in Rites of Spring's expanded look at the system and a distressingly common fear behind the Lost's muddled memories of Arcadia?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Much in the way victims of traumatic events often talk about reliving the event, this is a far more potent recollection than merely \u201cmemory.\u201d The changeling recalls every detail with perfect precision, and for all intents and purposes actually experiences it again. In fact, the memory is so vivid that <b>many changelings [\u2026] begin to doubt whether they ever escaped at all.</b> [\u2026] As a changeling\u2019s Clarity drops lower and lower, [\u2026] the doubts begin to pile up more, until <b>at Clarity 0 the changeling is utterly convinced that she remains a captive in Faerie.</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Years in the Everglades, living like a fugitive (and sometimes like an animal) has worn on Rose\u2019s Clarity. The constant press of the wetlands reminds her uncomfortably of her time in Faerie, and her self-control is beginning to crack. <b>Sometimes she dreams that she never left her master\u2019s garden, and that her life in Miami has been a cruel trick.</b> Sometimes, she dreams that she has been chosen as a kind of messiah, fated to deliver Miami from the tyranny of Summer. As these delusions gain hold on her mind, there\u2019s no telling what she might try. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Cerastes isn\u2019t entirely convinced that any of this is real.</b> Sometimes, that uncertainty paralyzes him with fear, and sometimes it makes him excessively reckless \u2014 <b>after all, if he\u2019s still trapped in his Keeper\u2019s den, what does he have to lose?</b> Paranoia aside, he tends to look out for number one first and foremost. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Autumn Nightmares p100</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Changeling, where <b>so much of the theme rests on the possibility that this might all be just a dream or a delusion,</b> the notion that the foil is not just a similar character but is a virtually identical copy is highly appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then, keyed off of the thing that keyed me off initially:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killer300</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/233636-integrating-oneiromancy-into-changeling-2-0?p=233693#post233693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hedge, Fae, and Wyrd, its worth pointing out, have rules, through Contracts. <b>Dreams distinctly do not.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;In dreams, we travel from location to location without any recollection of travel. <b>In dreams, the rules of the world are different, and we know that things have always been the way they are</b>: we always know that our fingers were made of jointed steel, or that we could fly, or that we are the best friends with Diana, who did not die, and who is just in hiding. In dreams, words and objects and places mean different things and have different connections. <b>Dreams have their own rules, which must be followed.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> The True Fae are out-and-out solipsists. This is Corebook Chapter One data on the same page as the bit directly above. That in mind, what seems to be practically the go-to reaction in fiction to characters being told the world they live in is a dream? (It is, with unastonishing regularity, typically not a sudden display of wholesale reality-warping, because the tacit assumption both in the trope itself and in Changeling's approach to oneiromancy is that the character is a <i>participant</i> in the dream, not a levelbreaker-swinging god-wizard shooting unreal power out of the top of their own skull like a geyser - that's more the Gentry's province, and even They largely interface with the niceties of oneiric stage convention.)<br /> <br /> The answer is almost categorically, as above, either sudden crippling anxiety about the fact that <i>anything could happen</i> or maybe-immediate-maybe-gradual wild abandon because <i>anything goes</i>.<br /> <br /> Does this sound familiar?<br /> <br /> The idea behind the latter mode of action, incidentally, is predicated upon a notion that the things and people in dreams <i>don't matter</i>, are <i>less real</i>, that the newly-&quot;awakened&quot; &quot;lucid dreamer&quot; is somehow <i>more than</i> these simulacra of things-to-care-about, that getting too attached to them will <i>ruin the fun</i> of whatever course of action one settles upon, which is important because the dream could suffer an interruption at any moment from an accident of timing or the intrusion of the real world or the rebellion of whatever bogies your imagination (or somebody else's imagination?) cooks up.<br /> <br /> <i><a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/thekeeper.png\" target=\"_blank\">Does this sound familiar?</a></i><br /> <br /> &quot;They are Faerie, and the land is Faerie.&quot; And is it any wonder, then, that the defense mechanism of most newly-wayward Lost is to forget about the details of their stay, to banish that dark-and-stormy-night of the soul to the mnemonic recesses of it-was-all-just-a-dream, and that rising Wyrd comes with greater fluency in the language of the unconscious, more potent evocation of the magics of Arcadia, and stronger recollections of dream and Durance alike?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>tl;dr When you're dealing with a perpetual dance on the threshold of unreality and wonder and people who have trouble with the experience of total life upheaval it does your gameline good to have a means of engaging with the most common narrative mechanism for moments of &quot;Did that actually happen?&quot; that the most widely-experienced altered state of consciousness inspires.</b><br /> <br /> Anyway, I've gotta get back to catching up on Halloween videos on Youtube. Fifteen more hours to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-08-2014, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T00:31:22-07:00","id":294597,"title":"","content":"Not read all the topic but I have idea for simple solution why Lost expert so much on Oneiromancy - <b>When in Durnace, you must <i>dream</i> your way home.</b> You must remember that your were human, and understand that all around you was a &quot;real bad dream&quot;. When life in Arcadia is taking hold on you, only in dreams you can remeber you were morals once, nor you Kith or Seeming. And by understanding those dreams, by working with them, you get your psychic at least to try to break free. To be literal - <b>When you become living tool in the hand of Gentry, you must <i>dream</i> your escape. </b>I could even seen something like Arcadia-bound changling going to the dreams of people on request of their Keeper, and after confronation with humanity dreams, they remeber being humans. <b>From dreams they get <i>idea</i> to even return to home.</b><br /> <br /> On Earth, Oneiromancy it is repeting this process. It also goes with it's own boons, but many Lost just start to make it becuase it led themselves to freedom and remebering previous life as humans. <b>In the dreams you are working your long forgotten memories.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}